| **Non-performance reason to migrate** | .NET Framework 4.8 reaches mainstream support end soon; security updates will cease |

> **My recommendation:** If your project has moderate complexity and you're already planning a .NET upgrade for other reasons, migrate to `System.Text.Json` but budget **20–40% extra time** for edge-case fixes. If the project is stable, low-traffic, and heavily reliant on dynamic/circular structures, keep Newtonsoft via NuGet package — it works fine on .NET 7 and saves you migration risk.

