## Migration Strategy Recommendations

### Phase 1: Measure Your Actual Workload
Don't guess. Instrument your current application:

```csharp
// Add this to critical paths to measure actual impact
using System.Diagnostics;
using System.Text.Json;

var sw = Stopwatch.StartNew();
var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(yourObject, _jsonOptions);
sw.Stop();
_logger.LogInformation($"Serialization took {sw.ElapsedMilliseconds}ms");
```

Profile with **dotnet-trace** or **Visual Studio Profiler** to see:
- Total time spent in JSON serialization
- GC collection frequency related to JSON allocs
- Which types are the hotspots

### Phase 2: Start with Source Generation

```csharp
// Define a context for all your frequently serialized types
[JsonSerializable(typeof(Order))]
[JsonSerializable(typeof(List<Order>))]
[JsonSerializable(typeof(OrderItem))]
[JsonSerializable(typeof(Product))]
[JsonSerializable(typeof(ShippingInfo))]
[JsonSerializable(typeof(Address))]
internal partial class AppJsonContext : JsonSerializerContext
{
}

// Use it everywhere instead of global options
var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(order, AppJsonContext.Default.Order);
var order = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<order>(json, AppJsonContext.Default.Order);
```

> **Critical:** You must add *every* type that appears in your serialization paths. Missing types fall back to reflection, killing performance. This is the #1 mistake teams make during migration.

### Phase 3: Parallel Run Comparison

Run both serializers side-by-side in staging:

```csharp
public interface IJsonSerializer
{
    byte[] Serialize<T>(T obj);
    T Deserialize<T>(byte[] data);
}

public class NewtonsoftSerializer : IJsonSerializer
{
    private static readonly JsonSerializerSettings Settings = new()
    {
        Formatting = Formatting.None,
        ContractResolver = new CamelCasePropertyNamesContractResolver(),
        // Copy your existing settings exactly
    };

    public byte[] Serialize<T>(T obj) =>
        Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(JsonConvert.SerializeObject(obj, Settings));

    public T Deserialize<T>(byte[] data) =>
        JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<T>(Encoding.UTF8.GetString(data), Settings);
}

public class StjSerializer : IJsonSerializer
{
    private readonly JsonSerializerOptions _options;

    public StjSerializer(JsonSerializerOptions options) => _options = options;

    public byte[] Serialize<T>(T obj) =>
        JsonSerializer.SerializeToUtf8Bytes(obj, typeof(T), _options);

    public T Deserialize<T>(byte[] data) =>
        JsonSerializer.Deserialize<T>(data, _options);
}
```

A/B test in production behind a feature flag. Compare:
- End-to-end request latency
- P95/P99 latencies (not just averages)
- Memory pressure and GC pauses
- Error rates

### Phase 4: Handle Edge Cases

| Issue | Newtonsoft Behavior | STJ Fix |
|-------|--------------------|---------|
| `DateTimeOffset` formatting | ISO 8601 by default | Explicitly set `WriteIndented = false` and verify output |
